{# The `OnFailure=` of storage-maintenance.service, and nothing else: one mail saying the
   nightly run could not even start. It exists because `Requires={{ pool_unit }}` turns an
   array that did not come up into a start job that fails before ExecStart=, which is the
   one failure the run cannot report on its own.

   It also fires when the run is killed -- a systemd stop or a timeout mid-sync -- in which
   case the wrapper's own mail and this one both arrive. Two mails about a failed night is
   the right side to err on. #}
[Unit]
Description=Report a storage maintenance run that could not start

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/opt/storagebaby/maintenance/storage-maintenance-failed.sh storage-maintenance.service
